# #60 — mitigate the two Cortex-A72s that are hotplugged at ~240 s.
#
# MT6797 boots on eight Cortex-A53s and onlines the A72s far too late for the
# arm64 capability machinery, which detects LOCAL_CPU_ERRATUMs across the boot
# CPUs and patches their alternatives once. Without this the A72s join carrying
# Spectre-v2/v3a/v4/BHB and errata 1742098 and 1319367 that nothing enabled, and
# `patches/v6.6/arm64/0001` lets them run unmitigated (which is honest — see
# /sys/devices/system/cpu/vulnerabilities — but is a cost).
#
# With this set, `patches/v6.6/arm64/0003` and `0004` detect all six during boot
# from the device tree's cortex-a72 node, so the alternatives are patched before
# the A72 exists and its cpu_enable() does something real.
#
# Turning it OFF again needs `# CONFIG_ARM64_MITIGATE_LATE_CPUS is not set`
# here, not deleting the file: merge_config only ever adds.
CONFIG_ARM64_MITIGATE_LATE_CPUS=y
